  "description": "BioMedLM 2.7B is a Stanford CRFM and MosaicML biomedical GPT-style language model trained on PubMed abstracts and full-text data from The Pile. This Forge entry is a non-routable onboarding manifest for the existing Forge-owned life-science transformer wrapper and digest-verified regional images. The 2026-06-03T13Z pass refreshed the public Hugging Face artifact state, moved wrapper caches from the image filesystem to /mnt/data, added an explicit research-use acknowledgement to the playground request contract, live-upserted the hidden row, and completed the first B200/us-central1 onboarding benchmark with 3 warmups and 10 measured requests. The upstream model card says the model is research-oriented and strongly recommends against production natural-language generation use; the BLOOM Open RAIL-M license also restricts medical advice and medical results interpretation. Keep this entry non-public until Forge completes safety/product review and the remaining GPU matrix validation.",
